Dragon Blast (2026-11-13): the Renut on Raging Blast 2 (default.xex USA Rev 1, XDK 2.0.12625), over Dragon Burst's
patches/renut 0001-0120 (Burst Limit's layout).

The device is a third layout: N&B's up to 10943, then +176 (bound objects to InKickOff), +212 (command buffer to the
gamma ramp), +216 (Swap count on); BehaviorFlags 24200, 0x5F00 bytes. The hooks at RB2's addresses; the device
creation is the hook on the hardware setup 0x824ABAE8 (RB2's Direct3D_CreateDevice 0x8249AD90 calls it for the
title device, as Burst Limit's), plus the no-hardware path 0x824ABD50 for the two devices of type 2 on which the game
records its command buffers (N&B's command buffer hooks, bound for the first time). RB2 has MGR's InsertCallback and
XGRegisterPixelShader again, no BeginVertices; its game initializes vertex declarations through 0x8249E900.
Evidence: docs/renut/HOOKMAP_RB2.md. Made by tools/renut/rb2_layout_edit.py.

